<title>USA: Maryland cigarette tax increase advances in House.</title>
<headline>Maryland cigarette tax increase advances in House.</headline>
<dateline>ANNAPOLIS, Md. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maryland House Ways and Means Committee has approved a proposal to raise the state's cigarette tax by 15 cents a pack.</p>
<p>The proposal would increase the tax to 51 cents a pack from 36 cents, raising $45 million of new revenues annually. It would divide the money between the state general fund and anti-drug and cigarette addiction programs.</p>
<p>Gov. Parris Glendening had sought to double the tax to 72 cents a pack. Supporters said even the lower tax hike approved by the Ways and Means Committee was expected to encounter strong opposition on the floor of the Hosue and Senate.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
